              <h2>The 6 Best Alternatives to Sago Mini World</h2>

              <!-- 1. KIDAMAME DISCOVERY -->
              <div class="app-review-card kidamame-pick">
                <div class="app-review-header">
                  <div>
                    <span class="app-pick-pill"><i class="fa-solid fa-star"></i> Best Next Step for Sago Mini Graduates
                      (Ages 4–10)</span>
                    <h3 style="margin-top: 0.6rem !important;">1. Kidamame Discovery</h3>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="app-specs-bar">
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-child"></i> Ages 4–10</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-infinity"></i> One-Time Purchase (No Subscription)</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-leaf"></i> 6 Biomes &amp; ~400 Facts</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-plane-departure"></i> 100% Offline</span>
                </div>
                <p>
                  If your child loved tapping every tree, cloud, and critter in <em>Sago Mini Forest Flyer</em> to see a
                  delightful animation, <strong><a href="/discovery/">Kidamame Discovery</a></strong> takes that exact
                  joy of tactile, rule-free exploration and elevates it for <strong>children ages 4–10</strong>.
                </p>
                <p>
                  Instead of fictional cartoon towns, kids explore <strong>6 real-world ecosystems</strong>: the Alps,
                  the African Savannah, the Australian Outback, the Arctic, the Sonoran Desert, and the Amazon
                  Rainforest. Every scene is packed with 20+ interactive elements: tap the ostrich to watch its eggs
                  tumble, touch the volcano to trigger an eruption, or watch a glacier calve into the Arctic sea!
                </p>
                <ul>
                  <li><strong>Grows With Your Child:</strong> Younger kids (4–6) love the gentle animations, authentic
                    animal calls, and co-reading with a parent. Older kids (7–10) dive independently into the
                    <strong>~400 "Did You Know?" cards</strong>.</li>
                  <li><strong>100% Offline &amp; Travel-Ready:</strong> All 6 biomes in Kidamame Discovery live right
                    on your device for instant airplane-mode play.</li>
                  <li><strong>No Monthly Fees:</strong> Try it for free, and unlock the entire app forever with a single
                    one-time purchase.</li>
                </ul>
                <%- include('../../partials/guide-kidamame-gallery') %>
              </div>

              <!-- 2. TINYBOP -->
              <div class="app-review-card">
                <div class="app-review-header">
                  <div>
                    <span class="app-pick-pill neutral">Best for Deep STEM Sandboxes</span>
                    <h3 style="margin-top: 0.6rem !important;">2. Tinybop (Coral Reef, Mammals &amp; Weather)</h3>
