                </div>
                <div class="app-specs-bar">
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-child"></i> Ages 4–10</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-tag"></i> Individual One-Time Purchases</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-microscope"></i> Science Exploration</span>
                </div>
                <p>
                  For kids who loved Sago Mini's "touch and see what happens" mechanics, Brooklyn studio <a
                    href="https://tinybop.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Tinybop</a> offers interactive
                  science models where children can experiment with weather systems, marine life in a coral reef, or how
                  mammals see, eat, and run.
                </p>
                <p>
                  <strong>Why Sago Mini fans love it:</strong> Just like Sago Mini, Tinybop apps never rush kids with
                  timers or grade them with quizzes. Instead, children learn by tinkering directly with working biological
                  and physical systems, making it a wonderful bridge from toddler pretend play to elementary STEM.
                </p>
              </div>

