                  Canadian studio <a href="https://playpokpok.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Pok Pok</a>
                  offers an even calmer, Montessori-inspired digital toy room with wooden-style busy boards, marble
                  runs, drawing pads, and quiet town scenes.
                </p>
                <p>
                  <strong>Why Sago Mini fans love it:</strong> Winner of an Apple Design Award, Pok Pok uses soft,
                  hand-recorded acoustic sound effects and muted colors so kids can play without getting wound up.
                  (Looking to avoid subscriptions? Check our <a href="/guides/pok-pok-alternatives/">Pok Pok
                    Alternatives guide</a>.)
                </p>
              </div>

